From 9411ae6a8c17d8324d49ebf872df2ebbe7c027a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fantasim <siuol@gmx.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 07:52:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(edit): an Undo restores each driver before the values it
 types

Symptom: the Undo of `[set goal collect, set target 25]` failed V1, because
target was restored before its discriminant; with `[set target X, set goal
collect]` the Undo applied but left X.
Cause: inverses were listed in plain reverse op order with cascade inverses
last, so an inverse could recreate an in-request state where a dependent
value does not fit its new driver, and a cascade inverse ran after the
field's own inverse.
Fix: each op's inverses form a group with its path, reach and drivers; a
group whose driver an earlier op changed after the group's value was last
written is placed right after that op's inverses (API.md E22, E15, E16;
log-2026-09-29 U-E22).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
